# The chunkah image (github.com/coreos/chunkah) that `just rechunk` splits every built image into layers with. ONE place for the pin:
# KEY=VALUE lines, parsed (never sourced) by .github/scripts/chunkah-ref.sh, which VERIFIES the cosign signature of the digest (keyless:
# the GitHub Actions OIDC issuer and an identity under github.com/coreos/chunkah/) before the recipe uses it. The tag is only a label
# for humans, the digest decides. The weekly bump-pins.yml moves the digest to `latest` after verifying its signature (bump-pin.sh chunkah).
# The same image Universal Blue's Aurora pins (image-versions.yml) at the first adoption.
CHUNKAH_IMAGE=quay.io/coreos/chunkah
CHUNKAH_TAG=latest
CHUNKAH_DIGEST=sha256:71e593421c5de7dcc7c8c5c50e98d3bac572055a76f399f61a491d123c20a523
